        "original_id": "e1f282a3-1403-5859-a32f-c987edd1fe22",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kenji Mizoguchi, David Wall, Kōzaburō Yoshimura\n- Films: Noëlle, An Osaka Story\n- Roles: film director, screenwriter, actor, producer\n- Awards: Best Director Award, Fort Lauderdale International Film Festival\n\nFacts:\n- Kenji Mizoguchi was born on May 16, 1898, and he was a Japanese film director and screenwriter.\n- David Wall wrote, produced, and directed the 2007 American dramedy film Noëlle.\n- Noëlle won the Best Director Award at the Fort Lauderdale International Film Festival.\n- An Osaka Story is a 1957 black-and-white Japanese film directed by Kōzaburō Yoshimura.\n- An Osaka Story was based on a story by Kenji Mizoguchi.\n- Kenji Mizoguchi died on August 24, 1956.",
